{"text": " You wake up in 1500 in London. It's mid-Summer Eve. You can smell wood smoke and the streets are glowing with fire light. Did you know that almost everyone you'll ever meet believes the sun goes around the earth? That's what Ptolemy taught about 1400 years ago. So what is the sun to you? Simple. It's the difference between day and night. Daylight is for work. Darkness is for sleep and prayer. But tonight, nobody sleeps. Doors are hung with green birch and flowers. Glass lamps burn all night. Neighbors share bread and drink by the bonfires. Why? A London writer John Stowe later wrote that a great fire could purge the infection of the air. Far away, a young Polish astronomer, Copernicus, is studying the sky. In 1543, the year he dies, his book puts the sun at the center and sets the earth in motion. And within 70 years, a new instrument will show you something shocking. The sun isn't perfect.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.86, "text": " You wake up in 1500 in London.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 22671, 294, 7042, 13, 50482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15880050659179687, "compression_ratio": 1.5864406779661018, "no_speech_prob": 0.03595209866762161, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.6182741522789001}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9916355609893799}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.46, "probability": 0.9986109733581543}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.9858765006065369}, {"word": " 1500", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.98, "probability": 0.720344603061676}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.98, "end": 1.6, "probability": 0.9096730947494507}, {"word": " London.", "start": 1.6, "end": 1.86, "probability": 0.9925447106361389}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.4, "end": 3.34, "text": " It's mid-Summer Eve.", "tokens": [50482, 467, 311, 2062, 12, 50, 30906, 15544, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15880050